processPipelineMethod(selector, arguments) -> Process or stage exit Array
    Require nonempty Array of argument Arrays; every executable and argument is a string.
    Expose stage exit statuses independently of aggregate wait.
processStartPipeline(stages, directory, outputPath)
    Snapshot environment and input. Create commands with a common working directory and separate job groups.
    Connect adjacent stages with operating-system pipes, keeping intermediate bytes outside capture limits.
    Feed configured text to the first stage. Capture the last stage or stream it to outputPath.
    Capture all standard errors in the normal bounded error stream.
    Start every command, then close parent pipe handles and publish the running job.
    On launch failure, close handles, kill and reap every started stage, and report the failed stage and command.
waitPipeline(state, commands)
    Reap every stage and publish its status. Aggregate using the rightmost nonzero exit; all zero yields zero.
    Mark the job finished only when all children have completed.
